    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** as the primary anchor. With an elite efficiency score of 81.88, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a high-leverage matchup against Severino; his aggressive slot in the leadoff position, combined with a 16% park factor boost and dynamic platoon advantage, makes him our clear catalyst for power and stolen bases. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** presents a top-tier start (73.10) against Alcantara. The 14% platoon boost and Alcantara's higher-than-average delivery time create a prime environment for **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** to exploit the basepaths, a critical component given our team\u2019s emphasis on the scarcity of SB. **Kyle Tucker** and **Jackson Merrill** also carry strong projections, both clearing the 65-point threshold as their respective matchups against Elder and Leahy offer the highest ROI for counting stats.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's card involved the utility spot, where **Josh Jung** (55.44) just edged out **Nasim Nunez** (53.72). While **Nasim Nunez** offers premium speed upside\u2014a category we consistently overweight\u2014his projection was hampered by an unfavorable 9th-order placement, which limited his run-scoring potential. Conversely, **Josh Jung** benefits from a more favorable lineup position and a steady matchup against Taillon, providing a higher floor for RBI and HR production. We continue to monitor **Heliot Ramos**, whose marginal score of 49.70 is salvaged by a wind-out projection, though he remains a player we are watching closely for signs of fatigue.\n\nRisk management remains a priority for the Austin Waves today. While the matchups are generally favorable, we have flagged **Sam Antonacci** as a high-risk play. His efficiency is dragged down to 46.73 by a difficult date with Gilbert, whose profile presents a significant hurdle for base-hit accumulation. Furthermore, we are keeping a close eye on the catchers, **Liam Hicks** and **Drake Baldwin**; both are currently operating in the 50-52 efficiency range. While they provide necessary positional depth, their scores are heavily dependent on platoon variables. We will be closely monitoring the final lineups to ensure no late-hour shifts occur, particularly as we look to maximize our limited game caps while **Luis Robert Jr.** remains sidelined on the IL.",
